From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bullhead-linux <kaiwalyakhasnis57@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:34:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a4xx: add the Adreno 418 (MSM8992)

The MSM8992 GPU, as the downstream 3.10 kgsl driver (adreno-gpulist.h,
adreno_a4xx.c) runs it: chip id 4.1.8.0, a420 PM4/PFP microcode, 512 KiB of
GMEM in OCMEM, and the A430 code paths: A430 VBIF settings, 7 UCHE ways for
the VFD, SP/TP software collapse control, the no-bootstrap-speed-up chicken
bit (CP_DEBUG bit 14). The wait for SP/TP power on, an endless loop so far,
gives up after 10 ms. OCMEM is looked up on the GPU's node ("sram"), not
the display controller's. The register dump leaves out the VMIDMT, XPU and
SMMU blocks, which are TrustZone's here (reading them is an external abort).

The GPU sits in the OXILI_GX GDSC, which sits on the VDD_GFX rail (an RPM
corner, rpmpd MSM8994_VDDGFX). Two power domains are not attached by the
driver core, so a4xx_gpu_init attaches the list itself, linked to runtime
PM; the rail's corner comes from the node's required-opps.

The GPU's SMMU belongs to TrustZone (qcom,iommu-secure-id, 18 here) and has
no mainline driver; the GPU then runs from the VRAM carveout. That SMMU
still loses its secure configuration at every GPU power down, and the CP's
first fetch then hangs the whole bus: restore it at every resume
(restore_sec_cfg), after setting up TrustZone's secure page table pool once,
as downstream does at boot, without which TrustZone refuses the restore.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_catalog.c |  11 ++
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c     | 163 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.h     |   6 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.h   |   5 +
 4 files changed, 173 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

